<title>USA: May paper Brent slips in late U.S. trading.</title>
<headline>May paper Brent slips in late U.S. trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paper Brent slipped in late U.S. trading on Thursday, with a European major attributed with all of the selling, traders said.</p>
<p>May Brent partials changed hands three times at $19.32 and once at $19.36.</p>
<p>London's IPE settled at $19.41 for May.</p>
<p>An April/May spread traded at plus 28 cents, down four cents from the lowest deal earlier in the day.</p>
<p>June/July traded twice at plus four cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
